[cot:thought] timeline: 2019 baseline at ~24???25 mph and 22???24 hr dwell; 2020 COVID mixed results; 2021???2022 service crisis with NS velocity falling to ~18???20 mph and dwell spiking above 30 hr; 2021???2022 revenue/carload rates rising sharply; 2023???2024 recovery where dwell improved faster than velocity; 2025???2026 velocity still trailing 2019 on key corridors and at Chicago.
[cot:thought] The headline narrative
[cot:thought] frames velocity recovery as slower than rate growth: shippers paid more while trains ran slower through 2022, and even after 2024 recovery, revenue/carload remained elevated while system speed only partially regained 2019 levels.
